"Alexa, ask Encore to search for Dune" runs Kodi's [Global Search](https://kodi.wiki/view/Add-on:Global_Search) add-on by default. Global Search draws its window from the skin's `script-globalsearch.xml`, and a skin that doesn't ship one, such as Arctic Fuse 3, gets Global Search's own default look, which stands out from the rest of the skin.

Skin search opens the skin's own search window instead, with what you said filled in, for the skins listed below. On any other skin it runs Global Search as before.

## Turn it on

Set **Search** under **Settings** → **Features** ([`alexa.search_mode`]({{base}}/reference/configuration/#alexasearch_mode)) to **The skin's own search** (`skin`). The default, **Global Search** (`global_search`), always runs Global Search. Each Kodi instance can override it with **Search** in its dialog, or `search_mode` for an instance declared in config.

Encore asks Kodi which skin it's running with every search, so you can change skins at any time without telling Encore. The instance dialog shows the skin Kodi is running now and what a search does on it, for example *Arctic Fuse 3: skin search supported*, *Aeon Nox: SiLVO: already skins Global Search* or *Copacetic: no profile, so it uses Global Search*.

## What a search does

In skin mode, a search:

1. reads the active skin from Kodi (`lookandfeel.skin`);
2. looks the skin's add-on ID up in the table below, exactly;
3. checks that the add-ons the skin's search needs are installed and enabled;
4. opens the skin's search window, waits for it to appear, and fills in what you said.

If the skin isn't in the table, already skins Global Search, lacks an add-on its search needs, or a step fails or its window doesn't open within a few seconds, Encore runs Global Search instead, and says so in the [request log]({{base}}/guides/request-log/) entry's note, e.g. `skin search: skin.copacetic has no profile; used Global Search`. A skin search doesn't need Global Search to be installed; falling back to it does, and Alexa says so when it's missing.

JSON-RPC can't run Kodi's builtin commands or open a skin's custom windows, so Encore drives the skin through an add-on on the Kodi host: [Skin Variables](https://github.com/jurialmunkey/script.skinvariables) (`script.skinvariables`), which the skins below already depend on, or the skin's own helper add-on.

